# Licensing status

Copyright (c) 2026 NOAH-NULL and FALLEN contributors.
Copyright (c) 2026 Junior Atlas contributors.

## No license was granted by the upstream project

Junior Atlas is a derivative of the FALLEN Discord bot:

- Project: FALLEN
- Repository: https://github.com/NOAH-NULL/FALLEN
- Snapshot audited: commit `31c7e35` (default branch `main`)

As of the 2026-11-23 audit, the upstream repository contains **no LICENSE,
COPYING, or NOTICE file**, has no license metadata in the GitHub API
(`"license": null`), and has no license file anywhere in its commit history.
The upstream README says "See the repository license file for the current
licensing terms," but no such file exists.

Under copyright law, the absence of a license means that the upstream author
retains **all rights**. No permission is granted to copy, modify, sublicense,
or redistribute the upstream work, except for rights that GitHub's Terms of
Service independently provide to users of the GitHub service (for example,
viewing and forking within GitHub).

## Effect on this repository

This file is a factual notice. It is **not** an open-source license and it
does not grant any rights that the upstream copyright holder has not granted.

- The Junior Atlas modifications are likewise **All rights reserved**.
- Do not publish, distribute, sell, or sublicense this repository or a built
  artifact publicly until the repository owner has obtained written permission
  from the FALLEN copyright holder or the upstream project is released under a
  compatible license.
- If upstream later publishes a license, this file and `NOTICE.md` must be
  updated and the upstream license text preserved verbatim.
- Existing attribution and copyright notices in `NOTICE.md` must be retained in
  source distributions and derivative works.

## Third-party software

Junior Atlas depends on third-party Python packages that remain under their own
licenses. See `NOTICE.md` for the principal dependencies. Installing or
distributing those packages does not relicense them, and their bundled license
texts continue to apply.
